<title>CHILE: Chile's Masisa starts Peruvian operations.</title>
<headline>Chile's Masisa starts Peruvian operations.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean wood products manufacturer Maderas y Sinteticos SA, or Masisa, will open a branch in Peru with an initial capital investment of $15,000, the company said.</p>
<p>The office in Lima will be in charge importing and marketing of wood, fiberboard and similar products into the Peruvian market, Masisa said in a statement filed with the Stocks and Insurance Superintendent.</p>
<p>The new company will be called Maderas y Sinteticos del Peru SA. ((--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
